      "writtenOn": "2026-09-18T09:01:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I may be misreading which path you mean.\nBoth validators are on the configuration path only -- four call sites, all in handleAggregationSourceCollectionPost and handleAggregationSourcePatch, where a client is submitting these values.\nThe per-request path, prepareAggregationHeaders at redfish_aggregator.hpp, reports no errors at all: it gates the authorization header on !username.empty() \u0026\u0026 !password.empty() and otherwise forwards silently.\n\nIs the concern that this validation should not exist at all, or that a bad stored credential should surface somewhere other than a forwarded request?",
      "parentUuid": "4949e981_2e0d75bf",
      "revId": "1b31bf007003508e8de8c054f059d6d27ccf9e57",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
