      "writtenOn": "2026-09-17T19:17:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "LLM seems to think : is just disallowed entirely in basic auth, at least given that we\u0027re using ascii encoding.  In theory we probably should have more checks here:\n\n```\nFor the user-id, recipients MUST support all characters defined in the \"UsernameCasePreserved\" profile defined in Section 3.3 of [RFC7613], with the exception of the colon (\":\") character.\n```\n\nhttps://httpwg.org/specs/rfc7617.html",
      "parentUuid": "d01cc98c_8aa16f67",
      "revId": "1b31bf007003508e8de8c054f059d6d27ccf9e57",
